course: dictionary
lesson: 15182
title: A word for people who work at sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seafarer is a person who travels by sea. The word is built from sea and a word for traveller, so the clue is in the name. A seafarer is often a sailor whose life and job is on the ocean.
explain: Look at the clues in «The seafarer had spent twenty years on the ocean and knew every star in the sky.» The words on the ocean and knew every star tell you the seafarer spent most of their life at sea. Ask: what word would fit here? A sailor would fit, so seafarer must mean a person who travels by sea.
explain: Seafaring is the adjective form. In «a seafaring nation», the word describes a whole country whose people travel and work on the sea. Notice how the word changes its ending to describe a thing or a place, not a person.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, the chapter «Wayfarers All» introduces the Sea Rat, a seafarer who tells Ratty stories of ports around the Mediterranean. Ratty is so excited by the stories that he nearly leaves home to follow him.
fact: Seafarer means a person who travels by sea, especially a sailor whose life and job is at sea.
fact: Seafaring is the adjective: «a seafaring nation» is a country whose people travel and work on the sea.
fact: The Vikings, Phoenicians and Polynesians were great seafarers who crossed oceans.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the Sea Rat is a seafarer who tells Ratty tales of faraway ports.
fact: Seafarer is a noun: one seafarer, two seafarers.
exercise: «The seafarer had spent twenty years on the ocean.» What is a seafarer? | A machine that makes waves | A kind of sea fish | *A person who travels by sea | A large bird that nests on cliffs
exercise: Which word means a person who travels by sea? | Mountaineer | *Seafarer | Shepherd | Gardener
exercise: Ahmed says, «The seafaring nation built fast ships.» What does seafaring describe? | A country famous for making shoes | A country covered in mountains only | A country with no coastline at all | *A country whose people travel and work on the sea
test: «The Sea Rat was a seafarer who told Ratty tales of far-off ports.» Who was the seafarer in The Wind in the Willows? | *The Sea Rat, a sailor who told tales of ports | The Badger, who ran the wild wood | Toad, who drove fast motor cars | The Mole, who dug long tunnels
test: Which best describes seafaring life? | Growing vegetables in a garden | Living in a city far from any water | Looking after sheep on a hill | *Living and working on the sea
exam: Which sentence uses seafarer correctly? | The seafarer was a kind of cake we ate for tea | The seafarer lived on a mountain and never saw the sea | *The seafarer spent years sailing across the oceans | The seafarer was a tiny insect in the garden
